# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# A wall's masonry module (`bim_masonry.dl`), with the wall as its source. A
# wall without one has none, and its layer is chosen explicitly. Its first
# line lies on the chosen layer's exterior face: at the start, or offset
# from the finish. Its whole modules and rest follow from the wall:
# straight, at an angle, made longer and moved. Giving a module leaves the
# wall as it was. A layer not in the type is refused, and so is a first line
# beyond the face. Curved and leaning walls are unsupported. The module is
# kept through the native file and IfcX. The sizes are generic (a 210 mm
# module), not project data.
import examples/bim-slice/bim_masonry.dl
import examples/bim-slice/bim_file.dl
import examples/bim-slice/bim_ifcx.dl
import examples/bim-slice/bim_ifcx_read.dl

function check masonry case {boolean:condition} named {a string:label}:
    execute:
        if condition = false:
            print ((the string form of "FAIL: ") + label) as a line
            @intrinsic("call", "libc", "exit", nothing, 1)
        print ((the string form of "PASS: ") + label) as a line

# Whether `value` is `wanted` within a micrometre.
function masonry value {a 64 bit floating-point number:value} is near {a 64 bit floating-point number:wanted}:
    execute:
        return (the absolute value of (value - wanted)) < 0.000001

# Whether plan point `spotValue` is (ax, ay) within a micrometre.
function masonry spot {cad vector2:spotValue} lies at {a 64 bit floating-point number:ax} {a 64 bit floating-point number:ay}:
    execute:
        return (masonry value (spotValue's x) is near ax) and (masonry value (spotValue's y) is near ay)

# The module of wall `wallId` in `modelValue`.
function the module of wall numbered {a 64 bit integer:wallId} in {bim model record:modelValue}:
    execute:
        set found to the bim wall index of wallId in modelValue
        return the bim masonry of wall (the item at found's position in (modelValue's walls's values)) in modelValue

# Replaces wall `wallId` of `target` by `changed`.
function put masonry test wall {bim wall record:changed} numbered {a 64 bit integer:wallId} in {a pointer to a bim model record:target}:
    execute:
        set found to the bim wall index of wallId in (@intrinsic("dereference", target))
        replace item at index found's position in (target's walls's values) with changed

set modelValue to an empty bim model
set target to the address of modelValue
set ground to add bim level named (the string form of "Ground") at 1.0 with height 3.0 to target
set layerValues to an empty list of a bim layer record
append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the string form of "brick", 0.1)) to layerValues
append (@intrinsic("construct", a bim layer record, the string form of "block", 0.1)) to layerValues
set cavityType to add bim wall type named (the string form of "Two leaves 200") with layerValues to target
set straightWall to add bim wall typed cavityType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 0.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 2.0 and y 0.0) to target
set slantedWall to add bim wall typed cavityType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 10.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 13.0 and y 4.0) to target
set plainWall to add bim wall typed cavityType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 40.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 42.0 and y 0.0) to target

check masonry case (((the module of wall numbered plainWall in modelValue)'s status) = (bim masonry not chosen)) named (the string form of "a wall without a module has none")
check masonry case ((give bim wall plainWall masonry module (2100 as a 64 bit integer) on layer 2 from finish false offset (0 as a 64 bit integer) in target) = false) named (the string form of "a layer not in the type is refused")
check masonry case (((the module of wall numbered plainWall in modelValue)'s status) = (bim masonry not chosen)) named (the string form of "and the wall still has none")

# The outer leaf, 2 m: nine modules of 210 mm and 110 mm over, from the
# start's corner on the exterior face (100 mm right of the line).
check masonry case (give bim wall straightWall masonry module (2100 as a 64 bit integer) on layer 0 from finish false offset (0 as a 64 bit integer) in target) named (the string form of "the outer leaf is given a 210 mm module")
set straightModule to the module of wall numbered straightWall in modelValue
check masonry case ((straightModule's status = (bim masonry measured)) and ((straightModule's whole = 9) and (masonry value (straightModule's rest) is near 0.11))) named (the string form of "2 m: nine modules, 110 mm over")
check masonry case ((masonry spot (the bim masonry point 0 of straightModule) lies at 0.0 (-0.1)) and (masonry spot (the bim masonry point 3 of straightModule) lies at 0.63 (-0.1))) named (the string form of "its lines on the exterior face from the start")
set footSpot to the bim masonry spot 3 of straightModule
check masonry case ((masonry value (footSpot's z) is near 1.0) and (masonry value (straightModule's height) is near 3.0)) named (the string form of "its spots at the wall's foot, its height the wall's")
set straightFound to the bim wall index of straightWall in modelValue
check masonry case (masonry value ((the item at straightFound's position in (modelValue's walls's values))'s finish's x) is near 2.0) named (the string form of "the wall is left as it was")

# The inner leaf chosen instead: its exterior face on the line.
check masonry case (give bim wall straightWall masonry module (2100 as a 64 bit integer) on layer 1 from finish false offset (0 as a 64 bit integer) in target) named (the string form of "the inner leaf chosen instead")
check masonry case (masonry spot (the bim masonry point 0 of (the module of wall numbered straightWall in modelValue)) lies at 0.0 0.0) named (the string form of "its face is the inner leaf's")
ignore give bim wall straightWall masonry module (2100 as a 64 bit integer) on layer 0 from finish false offset (0 as a 64 bit integer) in target

# Made 2.1 m long: ten whole modules, nothing over.
set longer to the item at straightFound's position in (modelValue's walls's values)
set longer's finish to a cad vector2 with x 2.1 and y 0.0
put masonry test wall longer numbered straightWall in target
set longerModule to the module of wall numbered straightWall in modelValue
check masonry case ((longerModule's whole = 10) and (masonry value (longerModule's rest) is near 0.0)) named (the string form of "made 2.1 m long: ten modules, none over")

# Moved 5 m along and 2 m across: the lines go with it.
set moved to the item at straightFound's position in (modelValue's walls's values)
set moved's start to a cad vector2 with x 5.0 and y 2.0
set moved's finish to a cad vector2 with x 7.1 and y 2.0
put masonry test wall moved numbered straightWall in target
set movedModule to the module of wall numbered straightWall in modelValue
check masonry case ((movedModule's whole = 10) and (masonry spot (the bim masonry point 1 of movedModule) lies at 5.21 1.9)) named (the string form of "the wall moved, its lines go with it")

# At an angle, 5 m along (3, 4): 23 modules and 170 mm over; from the
# finish, 50 mm in: 23 and 120 mm.
check masonry case (give bim wall slantedWall masonry module (2100 as a 64 bit integer) on layer 0 from finish false offset (0 as a 64 bit integer) in target) named (the string form of "a wall at an angle is given the module")
set slantedModule to the module of wall numbered slantedWall in modelValue
check masonry case (((slantedModule's whole = 23) and (masonry value (slantedModule's rest) is near 0.17)) and (masonry spot (the bim masonry point 1 of slantedModule) lies at 10.206 0.108)) named (the string form of "at an angle: 23 modules, 170 mm over, along its face")
ignore give bim wall slantedWall masonry module (2100 as a 64 bit integer) on layer 0 from finish true offset (500 as a 64 bit integer) in target
set backwardModule to the module of wall numbered slantedWall in modelValue
check masonry case (((backwardModule's whole = 23) and (masonry value (backwardModule's rest) is near 0.12)) and ((masonry spot (the bim masonry point 0 of backwardModule) lies at 13.05 3.9) and (masonry value (backwardModule's lead) is near 0.05))) named (the string form of "from the finish, 50 mm in: 23 modules, 120 mm over")

# A first line beyond the face.
ignore give bim wall plainWall masonry module (2100 as a 64 bit integer) on layer 0 from finish false offset (30000 as a 64 bit integer) in target
check masonry case (((the module of wall numbered plainWall in modelValue)'s status) = (bim masonry off its face)) named (the string form of "a first line beyond the face is not measured")
clear bim wall plainWall masonry in target
check masonry case (((the module of wall numbered plainWall in modelValue)'s status) = (bim masonry not chosen)) named (the string form of "cleared, the wall has none")

# Kept through the native file and IfcX.
set reread to the bim model parsed from (the bim file text of modelValue)
set rereadModule to the module of wall numbered slantedWall in (reread's modelValue)
check masonry case ((reread's valid and (rereadModule's whole = 23)) and ((masonry value (rereadModule's rest) is near 0.12) and (masonry value (rereadModule's lead) is near 0.05))) named (the string form of "kept through the native file")
set native to the bim native text of ifcx (the bim ifcx text of modelValue identified as (the string form of "m.ifcx") for project (the string form of "m") by (the string form of "test") at (the string form of "2026-10-21T00:00:00Z"))
set fromIfcx to the bim model parsed from native's text
set ifcxModule to the module of wall numbered slantedWall in (fromIfcx's modelValue)
check masonry case ((fromIfcx's valid and (ifcxModule's whole = 23)) and (masonry value (ifcxModule's rest) is near 0.12)) named (the string form of "and through IfcX")

# Curved and leaning walls are unsupported, not measured as if straight.
set bentWall to add bim wall typed cavityType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 20.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 24.0 and y 0.0) to target
set bent to the item at (the bim wall index of bentWall in modelValue)'s position in (modelValue's walls's values)
set bent's bulge to 0.5
put masonry test wall bent numbered bentWall in target
ignore give bim wall bentWall masonry module (2100 as a 64 bit integer) on layer 0 from finish false offset (0 as a 64 bit integer) in target
check masonry case (((the module of wall numbered bentWall in modelValue)'s status) = (bim masonry curved)) named (the string form of "a curved wall is unsupported")
set leaningWall to add bim wall typed cavityType on ground from (a cad vector2 with x 30.0 and y 0.0) to (a cad vector2 with x 34.0 and y 0.0) to target
set leaning to the item at (the bim wall index of leaningWall in modelValue)'s position in (modelValue's walls's values)
set leaning's lean to 0.1
put masonry test wall leaning numbered leaningWall in target
ignore give bim wall leaningWall masonry module (2100 as a 64 bit integer) on layer 0 from finish false offset (0 as a 64 bit integer) in target
check masonry case (((the module of wall numbered leaningWall in modelValue)'s status) = (bim masonry shaped)) named (the string form of "a leaning wall is unsupported")
